WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.273
The deadline to vote

00:00:01.273 --> 00:00:03.060
Yep.
is around the corner,

00:00:03.060 --> 00:00:05.620
and I know this is a major cause of yours,

00:00:05.620 --> 00:00:09.770
and I think it's something that
everybody's concerned about

00:00:09.770 --> 00:00:11.940
right now, which is

00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:15.510
the number of people that
will decide this election,

00:00:15.510 --> 00:00:18.610
the number of people that
decided the last election

00:00:18.610 --> 00:00:22.260
was so razor thin that
everyone needs to understand

00:00:22.260 --> 00:00:23.830
how important their vote is.

00:00:23.830 --> 00:00:25.110
It's crucial.

00:00:25.110 --> 00:00:28.337
Oh, and you know, it amazes
me to hear people say,

00:00:28.337 --> 00:00:30.700
"Well, I didn't vote 'cause
I didn't think it mattered."

00:00:30.700 --> 00:00:35.220
And, as you mentioned, this last election,

00:00:35.220 --> 00:00:37.070
in some of the swing states,

00:00:37.070 --> 00:00:40.940
the margin of difference
was five votes per precinct.

00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:44.030
And that wasn't just unique
to this past election.

00:00:44.030 --> 00:00:47.700
I mean, I have been campaigning
in midterm elections

00:00:47.700 --> 00:00:51.050
and in the last several elections,

00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:52.830
and I've looked at the statistics,

00:00:52.830 --> 00:00:55.540
and every time you look
at the margin of victory,

00:00:55.540 --> 00:00:58.760
because we have such a
low voting percentage

00:00:58.760 --> 00:00:59.930
in this country,

00:00:59.930 --> 00:01:03.120
that for every election, at every level,

00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:07.800
we're talking about one,
two, five, 10, 50 votes

00:01:07.800 --> 00:01:09.780
that determine who your mayor is,

00:01:09.780 --> 00:01:11.010
who your governor is,

00:01:11.010 --> 00:01:14.910
who your council member is.

00:01:14.910 --> 00:01:17.610
So, every vote absolutely matters,

00:01:17.610 --> 00:01:20.170
and people just take this for granted.

00:01:20.170 --> 00:01:23.763
And then when it doesn't turn
out the way they had hoped,

00:01:24.830 --> 00:01:27.233
they're shocked and upset.

00:01:28.170 --> 00:01:30.030
But this is a democracy,

00:01:30.030 --> 00:01:32.670
and yes, sometimes it's frustrating,

00:01:32.670 --> 00:01:34.860
and sometimes it can be alienating.

00:01:34.860 --> 00:01:36.420
I get that,

00:01:36.420 --> 00:01:38.990
but I've also traveled the world,

00:01:38.990 --> 00:01:42.190
and I've seen other forms of government,

00:01:42.190 --> 00:01:44.230
and I wouldn't trade our democracy

00:01:44.230 --> 00:01:45.540
for anything in the world,

00:01:45.540 --> 00:01:47.330
but in order for it to work,

00:01:47.330 --> 00:01:51.040
we need active, engaged
and informed citizens

00:01:51.040 --> 00:01:55.330
who are ready to do the
one, pretty simple thing,

00:01:55.330 --> 00:01:56.820
which is vote.

00:01:56.820 --> 00:01:58.810
And you can mail it in. (chuckles)

00:01:58.810 --> 00:02:00.200
Yep.
You can stand in line

00:02:00.200 --> 00:02:01.080
if you want.

00:02:01.080 --> 00:02:02.610
You can vote early,

00:02:02.610 --> 00:02:04.610
you can do it all ways,

00:02:04.610 --> 00:02:07.120
yes, we could have more ways to vote.

00:02:07.120 --> 00:02:08.820
It could be easier,

00:02:08.820 --> 00:02:11.320
and hopefully with the right leadership,

00:02:11.320 --> 00:02:16.080
we'll get voting requirements
that will be easier.

00:02:16.080 --> 00:02:17.973
But right now, it's pretty easy.

00:02:17.973 --> 00:02:19.220
(laughs)
Yeah.

00:02:19.220 --> 00:02:21.950
It takes some planning,

00:02:21.950 --> 00:02:25.540
and people can get the
information they need,

00:02:25.540 --> 00:02:29.070
but we just can't afford for
people to take the attitude

00:02:29.070 --> 00:02:30.990
that voting doesn't count.

00:02:30.990 --> 00:02:32.783
It absolutely does.

